menu "CYB3RGUN module"

config CGMODULE_CHANNEL
    int "Fixed 2.4 GHz channel"
    range 1 13
    default 1
    help
        The room's channel, concept.md principle 4. The core overrides it
        with the channel message and the value is kept in NVS, so this is
        only the value a freshly erased board starts on. It must match the
        channel of the pistols.

config CGMODULE_SLOT
    int "This target's slot in the room plan"
    range 0 32
    default 1
    help
        Slots are counted from 1. The core overrides this with the beacons
        message. A pistol that identified no beacons sends slot 0, which
        every module acknowledges and forwards as unaimed.

config CGBEACON_SLOTS
    int "Targets sharing one multiplex period"
    range 1 32
    default 4
    help
        usb-protocol.md gives the module a slot and a period but no slot
        count, so the count is set here. The multiplex window is the period
        divided by this number. See D-009.

config CGMODULE_STATUS_PERIOD_S
    int "Seconds between status messages"
    range 1 3600
    default 30
    help
        usb-protocol.md section 3: status on request and every 30 s.

endmenu
